    {
     "ord": 2,
     "period": {
      "start": "1938-12-03",
      "end": "1939-09-07"
     },
     "periodStartPrecision": "day",
     "periodEndPrecision": "day",
     "heading": {
      "zh-Hant": "西盆半島軍事轉運站指揮官",
      "en": "Commandant at Westerplatte"
     },
     "body": {
      "zh-Hant": "IPN 條目寫明，他自1938年12月3日至1939年9月7日任西盆半島（Westerplatte）軍事轉運站（Wojskowa Składnica Tranzytowa）的指揮官。波蘭歷史博物館的文章稱，該站自1938年起的站長是蘇哈爾斯基少校，副手為弗蘭齊謝克·東布羅夫斯基（Franciszek Dąbrowski）上尉。IPN 的蘇萊亞文章稱，該處守了7天而非12小時；主持防務的蘇哈爾斯基在工事成為廢墟、敷料、糧食與彈藥短缺時決定投降。博物館文章又稱，德軍准許這名入俘的指揮官保留佩劍。",
      "en": "The IPN entry gives his term as commandant of the Military Transit Depot on Westerplatte as 3 December 1938 to 7 September 1939. The Museum of Polish History says the depot’s commandant from 1938 was Major Sucharski, with Captain Franciszek Dąbrowski as deputy. Włodzimierz Suleja (IPN) writes that Westerplatte held for seven days instead of twelve hours, and that Sucharski, leading the defence, decided to capitulate once the fortifications lay in ruins and dressings, food and above all ammunition ran short. The museum article adds that the Germans let the commander, taken prisoner, keep his sabre."
     },
